.TH USB-IF 1 "September 2026" "cv-suite-automator 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
usb-if \- automate USB-IF CV Suite test runs and summarize existing results
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usb-if
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.PP
.B usb-if run
.I CHIPSET
.PP
.B usb-if parse
.I DIRECTORY
.PP
.B usb-if parse
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B usb-if
runs the interactive CV Suite automation workflow on a Windows 11 validation
host. It drives USB-IF CV Suite, controls the USB switchboard, and collects the
reports produced by the selected tests.
.PP
At startup, the program prompts for tests, host controllers, and USB protocol
modes. Press Enter at a selection prompt to select every available choice.
When both host controllers are selected, the operator is prompted once to move
the device between controller ports.
.PP
.B usb-if parse
is a non-interactive results command. It reads existing CV Suite HTML reports
for one product firmware version and creates a JSON failure summary without
initializing CV Suite or any lab hardware.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I CHIPSET
The bridge controller chipset name used to identify the test session, for
example
.BR 3861EN-FL .
.TP
.I DIRECTORY
A firmware-version results directory shaped as
.BR {results_drive}\eUSB-IF\ Results\e{product}\e{firmware_version} .
The directory must be exactly at the firmware-version level. A product
directory containing multiple firmware-version subdirectories, a capacity
directory, or a timestamped session directory is not accepted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show a concise usage summary for the selected command and exit without
initializing lab hardware.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
The automation command requires a Windows 11 validation host, USB-IF CV Suite,
an unlocked supported device, the Phidgets relay controller and USB2/USB3
switchboard, and the configured external results drive.
.PP
The
.B parse
command requires only read and write access to a populated firmware-version
results directory. It does not require a connected device, CV Suite, or the
switchboard.
.SH OUTPUT
Each run saves the CV Suite HTML reports and a
.B summary.json
file in a timestamped session directory on the configured results drive.
Reports are grouped by host controller and USB protocol.
.PP
The
.B parse
command reads all capacities, timestamped sessions, and HTML report attempts
under one firmware version. It writes
.B results.json
in that firmware directory, replacing an existing file atomically. The JSON
contains a
.B aggregate
object followed by a
.B capacities
object. Both sections group failures by operating system, USB controller, and
USB protocol. Each failure within those groups records
.BR suite ,
.BR test .
.PP
Aggregate entries additionally contain
.B occurrences
followed by a
.B DUTs
array.
It lists the unique, naturally sorted capacity-directory names that contributed
to that aggregate failure. Per-capacity entries contain neither occurrence
counts nor DUT lists.
.PP
Each capacity key is the complete capacity directory name, including a storage
vendor suffix when present. Capacities with no failures are included with an
empty object. The aggregate object sums matching failures across every capacity
and session while keeping operating system, controller, protocol, suite, and
test identity distinct.
.SH PARSE SEMANTICS
Individual failures come from CV Suite
.B Test-Fail
metadata. The occurrence count is the reported
.B Fails (N)
value, not merely the number of HTML files containing the test. If a failed
suite reports failures but identifies no individual test, its failures are
listed as
.BR Unattributed\ suite\ failure .
.PP
The known CV Suite noise messages
.B No MSC/BOT Device selected for testing.
and
.B No USB Device selected for testing.
as well as the message stating that no Enhanced SuperSpeed devices were
detected, do not create unattributed failures. Any separately attributed test
failures in the same report are still included.
.PP
Every failed report attempt is counted, including an attempt followed by a
passing rerun. Warnings and aborts are not counted as failures. Reports are
processed in deterministic order so repeated invocations over unchanged input
produce the same JSON content.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The selected command completed successfully, or help was displayed.
.TP
.B 1
The automation workflow could not continue.
.TP
.B 2
The command usage was invalid, the parse directory was not a firmware-version
directory, no recognizable CV Suite HTML reports were found, report metadata
was malformed, or
.B results.json
could not be written.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
uv run usb-if run "3861EN-FL"
uv run usb-if parse "M:\eUSB-IF Results\e3861EN-FL SECURE KEY 3.0\ev0706"
.fi
.SH LIMITATIONS
The workflow is Windows-only and depends on lab-specific hardware and CV Suite
window behavior. A physical cable move is required when both host controllers
are selected. The parser expects the directory hierarchy and HTML metadata
produced by CV Suite and does not infer exact tests from summary.json alone.
